When your c++ program runs , memory is devided into sections.
one of them is the code segment also called text segment.
This is where the actual machine instructions of the function are stored.
So, the functions code lives in the code segment.
This part of memory is read only so the program cannot modify its own code.
Think of it as : Blueprints stored safely in an library.
whenever you call a function the program creates a stack frame on the stack memory.
A Stack frame contains :
parameters
local variables
return address
temporary space for calculations
And when the function finishes :
its entire stack frame is deleted automatically.
Think of it as :
" A Temoporary workspace that appears during the function call and disappears when done."
